  "title": "Heo Nanseolheon",
  "summary": "Heo Nanseolheon (1563–1589), born Heo Chohui in Gangneung, was a Joseon-era poet who learned writing from her father Heo Yeop and poetry with Yi Dal. Her brother Heo Gyun compiled her poems after she died aged 27. A collection reached China in 1606 and was printed in Kyoto in 1711.",
